{"ratings":[{"id":"C1","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A persistent CI inspection error prevents later PR changes from being recorded."},{"id":"C2","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A valid repository registered with different capitalization can leave failing CI unclassified and block later PR observations."},{"id":"C3","consequence":"diag","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Failures also present on main are omitted from the diagnostic ledger."},{"id":"C4","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A later sibling-only attempt can hide the factory's completed rerun and leave classification pending."},{"id":"C5","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A completed skipped or neutral rerun remains pending indefinitely."},{"id":"C6","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A failing legacy status on main can be missed, causing an unnecessary PR rerun."},{"id":"C7","consequence":"bypass","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Rerunning a job can also run a dependent security job without checking whether that job is excluded."},{"id":"C8","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A Node test timeout can be classified as needing a fix instead of receiving the requested retry."},{"id":"C9","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A definitively rejected rerun remains claimed indefinitely and never produces a needs-fix result."},{"id":"C10","consequence":"diag","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A long setup preamble can displace the failure context from the feed excerpt."},{"id":"C11","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A passing line can collide across distinct failures and suppress a subsequent retry."},{"id":"C14","consequence":"outage","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Repeated unchanged inspections across paused PRs can exhaust the shared API allowance and disrupt observation."},{"id":"C11b","consequence":"diag","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A long setup preamble can displace the failure context from the feed excerpt."},{"id":"C12b","consequence":"diag","trigger":"normal","reason":"The extra additive migration is harmless structural churn with no demonstrated runtime failure."},{"id":"C7b","consequence":"bypass","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A rerun can execute a successful security-test step because the classifier ignores its metadata."}]}